// golden_test.go — T-48: the generated-golden differential for the
// reporadar module — the remote-URL grammar, the git blob SHA
// vectors, the diversified sampler, the candidate ranking, the
// dominance ladder's every verdict, the detection ladder's every
// honest line, the three slots together (incl. the never-raises
// doors), apply_detections' config mutations, the report lines, the
// quiet-startup gate, and the slot grammar.
//
// testdata/reporadar.golden.json is generated by
// testdiff/goldens/dump_reporadar.py from the unmodified reference
// (assadigit/GitCurator @ 98f4fc7, the pinned venv's CPython 3.12.15
// stdlib) — no per-run facts inside: every temp-vault path is folded
// to '<root>/…'; the sampler's trees are written in sorted name order
// so CPython's readdir order and Go's sorted ReadDir agree (the
// documented convergence).
//
// THE LAW: goldens are never hand-edited; a divergence is either a Go
// bug (fix the port) or a reference behavior change (regenerate + say
// so in the commit).
